to Woodland right now. It started the way a lot of things start with people trying to make more money. The grocery business decided that they needed some way to reduce their overhead. One of the main places they felt they were losing money was the checkout line. They came up with the idea of having some kind of a scannable code. Which would move people more quickly through the line. One of the first people that started working on it was an engineer named Joseph Woodland. After working on the Manhattan Project, Woodland moved on to develop an innovative way to produce
