The very first barcodes were in the shape of a bullseye. Actually, they didn't call them barcodes yet. Woodland's invention was called a classifying apparatus and method. I'm really glad that we don't call them that anymore. That was 1948, and then for about 20 years, the bullseye idea gathered dust. The scanners and other equipment needed to put the system in place were just too expensive for any of it to be feasible. Fast forward to 1973. The technology is now a bit more affordable and a group of
最早的条形码就是靶心形状的。实际上，他们当时还不叫它们条形码。伍德兰的发明被称为“分类装置和方法”。我真庆幸我们现在不这么叫它们了。那是1948年，随后的大约20年里，靶心这个创意一直被束之高阁。当时实施该系统所需的扫描仪和其他设备实在太昂贵了，根本不可行。快进到1973年。这项技术现在变得更加亲民了，以一个叫阿兰·哈伯曼的人为首的一群

