00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:36.000
When barcodes became the standard, they didn't just make check out lines faster. They allowed stores to keep track of huge amounts of inventory and to collect data on what we were buying. Data they could use to keep us coming back for more without barcodes. As super stores might not exist, but equally, you know, a small store might need more employees to run it. It's like the grease that makes the machine run. That's one of the key elements of efficiency in our capitalist system.
当条形码成为标准时，它们不仅使结账队伍变得更快。它们还允许商店跟踪巨量的库存，并收集关于我们购买行为的数据。这些数据可用于吸引我们不断回购。如果没有条形码，超级市场可能就不会存在；但同样地，一家小商店可能需要更多员工来运营。它就像是让机器运转的润滑油。这是我们资本主义体系中效率的关键要素之一。

