00:09:34.000 --> 00:10:13.000
Again, what we're talking about here is the UPC barcode that George Lourer invented. This is the barcode that you and I and everyone in the world has had the most interaction with. The UPC barcode is divided into two halves. It's actually two barcodes sitting right next to each other. You can see this visually because there are these longer bars that come down in the middle and on each side. Those are called the guard bars. The guard bars tell the scanner that the code is starting and ending. The left half of the barcode tells you who the manufacturer is, and the right half tells you which particular product it is. And this was something I didn't realize.
再次强调，我们在这里讨论的是乔治·劳勒发明的UPC条形码。这是你、我和世界上每个人接触最多的条形码。UPC条形码分为两半。它实际上是紧挨着彼此的两个条形码。你可以从视觉上看出这一点，因为在中间和两侧有一些向下延伸的更长的条。这些被称为警戒条。警戒条告诉扫描仪代码从哪里开始，到哪里结束。条形码的左半部分告诉你制造商是谁，右半部分告诉你具体是什么产品。这是我以前没有意识到的一点。

18
00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:52.000
The scanner is reading both the white and the dark lines. To understand the scanner, just consider yourself in a dark room where the wall behind you has bars painted on it. And you took a flashlight and shined it over your head across the bars. You would see the room get a little lighter when you were over the white bars and it would get dark when it was over the dark bars. Black lines that don't reflect the laser light back to the scanner register as a one. white lines equal zero. There are actually 95 evenly spaced columns on a UPC barcode. A thick black line is actually a bunch of ones right next to each other.
扫描仪同时在读取白色线条和黑色线条。为了理解扫描仪的工作原理，你可以把自己想象在一个黑暗的房间里，你身后的墙上画着条纹。你拿着手电筒，举过头顶从条纹上方照过去。当手电筒照在白色条纹上方时，你会看到房间变亮了一点，而在黑暗条纹上方时则会变暗。不反射激光回到扫描仪的黑色线条被记录为1，白色线条等于0。UPC条形码上实际上有95个均匀间隔的列。粗黑线实际上是一连串紧挨在一起的1。

19
