The computer adds all that together and you get a string of 12 numbers. This number goes to the computer. The computer now looks up in its table to get the information, such as what is the product, how much they're charging for it, but that is not in the barcode. The only thing that's in the barcode is where the computer should look. This number is also printed below the barcode just in case the scanner isn't working, which for me really makes the whole mystery a little anti-climactic. I mean, it's right there. So when most people until recently thought of barcodes they thought of something that was a combination of bars and stripes. More recently two
计算机将所有这些加在一起，你就会得到一串12位数字。这个数字会发送给计算机。计算机现在会在其表格中查找信息，例如这是什么产品，他们收取多少费用，但这些信息并不在条形码中。条形码里唯一的内容就是计算机应该去哪里查找。这个数字也印在条形码下方，以防扫描仪无法工作，对我而言，这确实让整个神秘感变得有点虎头蛇尾。我的意思是，它就写在那里。因此，直到最近，当大多数人想到条形码时，他们想到的都是条纹和线条的组合。最近，

